{
  "title": "Coupling-modulated ring, 106.25 GBd PAM4 flow (traveling-wave PN)",
  "group": "Lasers & modulators",
  "description": "Example 48 with traveling-wave PN phase shifters and real optical transit: each arm's junction sits under a transmission-line electrode (Z0 30 Ohm) fed through a 30 Ohm driver resistance and terminated into the bias (PN_B's p-side rail at 2*vbias, so both junctions share the bias), and the arms and ring guides carry their group delay (transit = delayed), so the ring has its real round trip and photon lifetime. A 10 um, 0.3 dB/cm feedback delay line closes the ring; the optimizer also sets the input coupler and the PRBS source's TX FFE pre/post-cursor taps (linear, relative to the main cursor). Same spec as example 48 (RLM > 0.95, TDECQ < 1.5 dB, relOMA > -2 dB, ER > 3.5 dB)",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -360,
        "title": "Coupling-modulated ring at 106.25 GBd — TW PN, real optical transit",
        "lines": [
          "Example 48 with traveling-wave PN arms and real optical transit.",
          "Each arm's junction sits under a TW electrode: an RLC ladder, one",
          "section per <= 100 um (unloaded n_rf 2.4, 2 dB/cm), loaded by the",
          "junction (Cj0 0.3 fF/um, 10 Ohm*mm series R), Z0 30 Ohm, fed by a 4 Vpp",
          "EMF behind 30 Ohm at e_in, terminated into the bias (VTERM = vbias).",
          "Push-pull: PN_A's line is its n side (ref = ground), PN_B's its",
          "p side (ref = VRAIL = 2*vbias, so both junctions sit at vbias).",
          "RF/optical walk-off modelled.",
          "Optics: transit = delayed on the arms and ring guides, so the ring",
          "has its real round trip (~7 ps) and photon lifetime (~6 UI) instead",
          "of a quasi-static resonance. Feedback delay line WG_R1 + WG_R2:",
          "10 um at 0.3 dB/cm (fixed).",
          "Optimizer: detune, bias, arm imbalance, PN length, termination,",
          "DC1 power coupling (k1) and the TX FFE taps ffe_pre / ffe_post",
          "(linear, relative to the main cursor; negative = de-emphasis).",
          "Z0 and the driver R are fixed at 30 Ohm; DC2 is fixed at k2 = 0.5.",
          "PRBS seed 5407 starts PRBS-13Q at symbol 4064, so the 1000-UI eye",
          "step holds its run of 6 zeros and of 7 threes: the optimizer scores",
          "OMA_outer / TDECQ_outer like the full-period evaluate.",
          "Start design, evaluated (full PRBS-13Q): relOMA -3.5 dB, ER 3.8 dB,",
          "RLM 0.89, TDECQ 3.6 dB -- ER passes, the rest miss (the previous",
          "start: -4.7 dB, 2.3 dB, 0.94, 2.9 dB; the same worst margin).",
          "Device-limited: the ring's photon lifetime (~5 UI) makes the",
          "reference equalizer boost by C_eq ~1.7 (~2.4 dB of TDECQ alone);",
          "6 Vpp drive or VpiL 1 V*cm still leave relOMA ~-3.5 dB, TDECQ",
          "~2.7 dB. The 1000-UI eye step reads RLM ~0.05-0.1 above the full",
          "period on this ring."
        ]
      }
    ],
